.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt SSMAMP 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssmamp
.Nd Analog Devices SSM3515 speaker amplifier
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "ssmamp* at iic?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Analog Devices SSM3515 mono class-D amplifier as a
digital audio interface device for a machine driver such as
.Xr applemacaudio 4 .
.Pp
The part has neither speaker sense nor a shutdown line, so nothing
watches the speaker and the only way to silence it is over I2C.
The driver follows the rules of
.Xr tasamp 4 :
.Bl -bullet
.It
The part is reset and recognised by its reset values, then kept powered
down, muted and at its lowest analog gain until the machine driver sets
a limit.
There is no default limit.
.It
The output for a full-scale input is never above the limit's cap: the
analog gain is chosen below it and the rest is taken off the digital
volume, which is never set above 0 dB.
The part's limiter holds peaks to the cap as well.
While the limit is locked the output is muted.
.It
Reads are done twice and compared, writes are read back.
Any I2C failure or mismatch mutes and powers down the part until the
system is restarted.
The part's own recovery from overcurrent, overtemperature and
undervoltage is set to manual, so it does not restart itself either.
.El
.Pp
The part takes one mono slot of a TDM frame at 48 kHz.
With I2S the frame must be inverted, since the part starts a TDM frame
on the rising edge of the frame clock.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr applemacaudio 4 ,
.Xr iic 4 ,
.Xr tasamp 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Nx 12.0 .
.Sh CAVEATS
Without sense data a speaker protection daemon has nothing to model, and
.Xr applemacaudio 4
does not unlock the speakers of machines built with this part.
